
                                                   FILLP COMMAND


Fills specified range with user defined byte value or default value "0x00".

Below is the syntax :
                                  fillp 	-addr address  -l len  [-fill fillValue] 

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES       |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -addr       |    Start address from where a particular pattern must be filled for specified length. Mandatory
               |    switch.
   -l          |    Specifies length for fill operation. Mandatory switch.
   -fill       |    One byte value. Default value 0x00. Optional field.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:
	read -in input1.hex
	fillp -addr 0x80001000 -l 0x20 -fill 0xFF
	write -out outputFile.hex -lyt 0x10	
